          <strong>Never used a spin wheel tool before?</strong> Start with our <a href="https://spinthewheelsonline.com/blogs/spin-the-wheel-tool">complete guide to what a Spin the Wheel tool is and how it works</a> — it walks through the randomness engine and a first-spin setup that takes under a minute.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ── Section 1 ── -->
      <h2 id="the-problem">1. Why "What's for Dinner" Is the Hardest Question of the Day</h2>

      <p>The trouble isn't a shortage of options — most households can name fifteen or twenty meals they'd happily eat again. The trouble is getting more than one person to land on the <em>same</em> meal, at the <em>same</em> time, while also accounting for what's actually in the fridge, how tired the cook is, and what got made three times already this week.</p>

      <p>Psychologist Barry Schwartz popularized the idea that having too many decent options makes choosing <em>harder</em>, not easier—because now you also worry about picking the "best" one. When literally anything sounds acceptable, nothing feels worth committing to, which is how "I'm fine with anything" turns into staring at the fridge until 7:30 p.m.</p>

      <p>A spin wheel sidesteps the whole standoff. Because every option on the wheel was added by agreement beforehand, the wheel isn't picking <em>for</em> anyone — it's just revealing which of the choices you already approved happens to be tonight's.</p>

