        <div class="callout-icon">⚠️</div>
        <div class="callout-body">
          <strong>Resist adding more than 16–18 entries at first.</strong> A wheel loaded with 35 options rarely lands on the same dish twice a month, which makes it feel random rather than useful. Start with 10–14 genuine favorites and expand slowly as you learn what actually gets picked and eaten.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ── Section 5 ── -->
      <h2 id="cuisines">5. Cuisine Wheels: For When You Want to Cook, Not Just Eat</h2>

      <p>If your household enjoys cooking and can improvise within a style, try a <strong>cuisine-first wheel</strong> instead of a dish-specific one. Rather than landing on "chicken tikka masala," the wheel lands on "Indian," and whoever's cooking decides the specific dish from there. This works especially well when one person genuinely enjoys the creative side of cooking — the wheel gives them a direction without dictating every ingredient.</p>

      <div class="wheel-setup">
        <div class="wheel-setup-title">🎡 Sample Cuisine Wheel</div>
        <ul>
          <li>Italian — pasta, pizza, risotto</li>
          <li>Indian — curry, dal, biryani</li>
          <li>Japanese — sushi, ramen, teriyaki</li>
          <li>Mexican — tacos, quesadillas, enchiladas</li>
          <li>Middle Eastern — kebabs, mezze, shakshuka</li>
          <li>Thai — green curry, pad thai, noodle salad</li>
          <li>Chinese — stir-fry, dumplings, fried rice</li>
          <li>Comfort classics — roast dinner, pie, mash</li>
          <li>Chef's choice — whatever inspires you tonight</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="article-img">
        <img src="/spin-the-wheel-button.webp"
             alt="Flat-lay of dishes from different world cuisines arranged around a cuisine-themed spin wheel"
             loading="lazy" width="1200" height="750"/>
      </div>

      <p>A cuisine wheel also naturally builds in variety. Because each spin lands on a whole food tradition rather than one dish, you're less likely to end up eating some variation of pasta four nights running without noticing.</p>

